@startuml
skin rose
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title DAP launch and lifecycle

start
:user triggers dap_start
(or DAP drawer "start");
:editorDapStartLaunch(launch_idx);
:editorDapShutdown — close any
prior adapter/PTY/owned pane;
:work on a local copy of the
launch config so console="terminal"
mutations stay out of E.dap_launches;
:editorDapPrepareTerminalConsole;
if (console == "terminal"?) then (yes)
	:editorTerminalPaneOpenSplit
	("sleep infinity") — split
	the focused pane horizontally,
	spawn placeholder so the slave
	tty stays open;
	:ptsname(master_fd) → /dev/pts/N;
	:set launch.tty = "/dev/pts/N";
	:E.dap_terminal_leaf = leaf;
else
	:strip console key so the
	adapter never sees it;
endif
:editorLspSpawnProcess on the
adapter command (gdb -i dap, etc.);
:send initialize request;
:send launch request with mutated
copy (tty included if applicable);
:DAP adapter spawns the inferior.
gdb-dap/lldb-dap honor the tty
field by attaching the inferior's
stdin/stdout/stderr to that pts;
partition "session" {
	repeat
		:editorDapPumpNotifications
		from editorRefreshScreen
		drains the adapter fd;
		:handle stopped/output/threads
		events;
	repeat while (E.dap_running)
}
:on "terminated" or "exited" event
(or editorDapStop / shutdown):
:editorDapShutdown;
:editorDapCloseOwnedTerminalPane —
verify leaf is still in the tree,
editorPaneTreeCloseLeaf, restore
focus to the surviving sibling;
stop

@enduml
